Q: Android NFC on physical devices A: <p>Your tag doesn't look like NDEF, so the callback may not trigger like this (techType for NDEF is &quot;android.nfc.tech.Ndef&quot;).</p>
<p>Try changing:</p>
<pre><code>NfcManager.registerTagEvent();
</code></pre>
<p>to</p>
<pre><code>NfcManager.registerTagEvent({
  isReaderModeEnabled: true,
  readerModeFlags:
    NfcAdapter.FLAG_READER_NFC_A |
    NfcAdapter.FLAG_READER_SKIP_NDEF_CHECK,
});
</code></pre>
<p>and instead of <code>tag?.ndefMessage</code> check, for example, <code>tag?.techTypes?.includes('android.nfc.tech.IsoDep')</code></p>

Q: QML set font capitalization A: <p>The proper way is acting through the <code>FontMetrics</code>. Wrapping the <code>FontMetrics</code> property to the parent component make it easily accesible from the outside</p>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>Text {
   property alias bold: fm.bold
   property alias italic: fm.italic
   property alias capitalization: fm.capitalization

  FontMetrics {
    id: fm
  }
}
</code></pre>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>MyText {
  capitalization: Font.AllUppercase
  bold: true
}
</code></pre>
